{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a comprehensive stitch task (Task #5632) to create differential tests for `cmd/chronic` covering srd112-chronic requirements R2.1, R2.2, and R2.3. The deliverable is a single file `cmd/chronic/chronic_test.go` that uses the project's differential testing framework (`pkg/testutils`) to compare the Go chronic binary against the Homebrew moreutils reference binary. The task title is \"[stitch] cmd/chronic differential tests (srd112-chronic R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\".\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against Homebrew reference binary\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` framework with `DiffTest` struct\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the Go binary under test\n   - Reference binary lookup via `exec.LookPath(\"chronic\")` (NOT g-prefixed — moreutils, not coreutils)\n   - Graceful skip when reference binary not installed\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for deterministic output\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - SRD requirements: R2.1 (exit with command's status), R2.2 (exit 100 on command not found), R2.3 (SIGPIPE handling)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd112-chronic.yaml` (read)\n     - Defines chronic's requirements: R1 (command execution/output suppression) and R2 (exit codes and SIGPIPE)\n     - R2.1: \"Must exit with the exit status of COMMAND\"\n     - R2.2: \"Must exit 100 when COMMAND cannot be found or executed\"\n     - R2.3: \"Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\"\n   \n   - `cmd/chronic/main.go` (read — existing implementation being tested)\n     - Already implements all R1 and R2 requirements\n     - Key functions: `run()`, `parseArgs()`, `executeCommand()`, `showOutput()`\n     - Uses `errors.AsType[*exec.ExitError](err)` to extract exit codes\n     - Returns 100 for command-not-found errors\n     - Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at program start\n     ```go\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         os.Exit(run(os.Args[1:]))\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-14.0.yaml` (read)\n     - Defines test cases: `chronic_success_suppressed` (echo hello → exit 0, no output) and `chronic_failure_shown` (false → exit 1, no output)\n     - Preconditions: Go binary built, reference binary from Homebrew moreutils, LC_ALL=C\n\n   - `cmd/chronic/chronic_test.go` (to be created)\n     - Must follow the standard differential testing pattern\n     - Must cover R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 test scenarios\n\n   - Package contract for `srd001-testutils`:\n     ```\n     DiffTest struct { Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }\n     RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n     BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string  // inferred from usage pattern\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Gathered all necessary context: SRD requirements, existing implementation, test suite spec, package contracts, and shared protocols\n   - Identified that chronic uses \"chronic\" as the reference binary name (moreutils), not a g-prefixed name\n   - Need to design test cases covering: successful command (exit 0), failing command (exit 1/non-zero), command not found (exit 100), and SIGPIPE handling\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The complete stitch task description with all project context, SRDs, architecture, constraints, execution constitution, and task requirements for creating `cmd/chronic/chronic_test.go`\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/chronic/chronic_test.go` with differential tests covering R2.1, R2.2, R2.3\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/chronic/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n   - Verify all 5 acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5) are met\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (SRD, main.go, test suite) and was about to write `cmd/chronic/chronic_test.go`. The test file needs to:\n   - Follow the standard `TestDiff` pattern with `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"chronic\")`\n   - Include test cases for R2.1 (exit with command status — test with `true` exit 0, `false` exit 1, `sh -c \"exit 42\"` for arbitrary codes)\n   - Include test cases for R2.2 (exit 100 for nonexistent command like `nonexistent_command_xyz`)\n   - Include test cases for R2.3 (SIGPIPE — already handled by InstallSIGPIPEHandler, but implicit in the binary behavior)\n   - Also include the test cases from test-rel-14.0.yaml: `chronic_success_suppressed` and `chronic_failure_shown`\n   - Use `LC_ALL=C` in Env field\n   - Start with copyright header per go_style_constitution\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the `cmd/chronic/chronic_test.go` file. The task description states: \"Files: path: cmd/chronic/chronic_test.go, action: create, note: Differential tests comparing Go chronic against Homebrew moreutils chronic\". The test must cover R2.1 (exit status passthrough), R2.2 (exit 100 on not-found), and R2.3 (SIGPIPE handling). Then run `go test ./cmd/chronic/... -count=1` to verify.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5632/11219621-a4aa-469f-8167-d9d655f0c002.jso