{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018UzSd2pvnJdCZhrWj677HD","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me provide you with a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Summary\n\nI found the differential testing pattern used throughout this repository and the copyright header specification. Here are the key findings:\n\n### Differential Testing Pattern Example\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5632/cmd/arch/arch_test.go`\n\nThis is the simplest example showing the pattern:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Implements srd045-arch R3.1-R3.3.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"garch\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n\t}\n\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t{Name: \"no_args\", ExitCode: 0},\n\t\t{Name: \"extra_operand\", Args: []string{\"extraarg\"}, ExitCode: 1},\n\t\t{Name: \"unknown_flag\", Args: []string{\"--unknown\"}, ExitCode: 1},\n\t}\n\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\n### Core Imports & Function Signatures\n\n**Import Path:**\n```go\n\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n```\n\n**Key Functions:**\n\n1. **BuildBinary** - Compiles a Go package and returns the binary path:\n   ```go\n   func BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\n   ```\n\n2. **RunDiffTests** - Executes differential tests comparing Go binary against reference binary:\n   ```go\n   func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n   ```\n\n**DiffTest Structure:**\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      int\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n### More Complex Example\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5632/cmd/cat/cat_test.go`\n\nThis shows the pattern with stdin tests, multiple flags, normalization, and additional test functions for edge cases (file handling, SIGPIPE).\n\n### Copyright Header Specification\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5632/docs/constitutions/go-style.yaml`\n\nThe copyright header format is specified as:\n\n```\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n```\n\n**Key requirements from go-style.yaml:**\n- Must appear on lines 1-2 (before package declaration)\n- Followed by a blank line, then the package clause\n- Applies to all Go files: hand-written (magefiles/), generated (cmd/, pkg/, internal/, tests/)\n\nThis constitution also documents the complete testing requirements, including use of table-driven tests with `t.Run`, `t.Parallel()` for safe-to-parallelize tests, and `t.Helper()` for test helper functions."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11219621-a4aa-469f-8167-d9d655f0c002","uuid":"d9328d9d-915d-4672-9252-f435c4f7a084","timestamp":"2026-05-28T16:55:27.946Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find an existing cmd/*/..._test.go file in this repo that uses the differential testing pattern with testutils.RunDiffTests. I need to see the exact import paths, function signatures, and test structure. Look for any test file under cmd/ that imports testutils. Show the full contents of one such file. Also check if there's a go_style_constitution file under docs/constitutions/ that specifies the copyright header format.","agentId":"a2a55656e69717760","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me provide you with a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Summary\n\nI found the differential testing pattern used throughout this repository and the copyright header specification. Here are the key findings:\n\n### Differential Testing Pattern Example\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5632/cmd/arch/arch_test.go`\n\nThis is the simplest example showing the pattern:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Implements srd045-arch R3.1-R3.3.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"garch\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n\t}\n\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t{Name: \"no_args\", ExitCode: 0},\n\t\t{Name: \"extra_operand\", Args: []string{\"extraarg\"}, ExitCode: 1},\n\t\t{Name: \"unknown_flag\", Args: []string{\"--unknown\"}, ExitCode: 1},\n\t}\n\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\n### Core Imports & Function Signatures\n\n**Import Path:**\n```go\n\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n```\n\n**Key Functions:**\n\n1. **BuildBinary** - Compiles a Go package and returns the binary path:\n   ```go\n   func BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\n   ```\n\n2. **RunDiffTests** - Executes differential tests comparing Go binary against reference binary:\n   ```go\n   func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n   ```\n\n**DiffTest Structure:**\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      int\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n### More Complex Example\n\n**File:** `/private